1
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Experience Earth like never before.

2
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
A Beautiful Planet is a documentary, adventure,
family film directed by Toni Myers.

3
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
A breathtaking portrait of Earth from space, providing a unique perspective and
increased understanding of our planet and galaxy as never seen before.

4
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Made in cooperation with the National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA), the film features stunning footage of our magnificent blue
planet — and the effects humanity has had on it over time — captured by the astronauts aboard the International Space Station (ISS).

5
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Self - Narrator (voice), played by Jennifer Lawrence.

6
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Self (uncredited), played by Samantha Cristoforetti.

7
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Self (uncredited), played by Scott Kelly.

8
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Self (uncredited), played by Kjell Lindgren.

9
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
A Beautiful Planet is an IMAX Entertainment documentary produced in collaboration with
NASA and filmed aboard the International Space Station by astronaut crews.

10
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Narrated by Jennifer Lawrence, it was produced and directed by Toni Myers.

11
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
The film offers distinctive views of Earth and provides insight into the day-to-day
activities of the crews, captured over fifteen months aboard the space station.

12
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
It also examines the impact of humans on Earth and its
potential analogues in the Milky Way.

13
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
A Beautiful Planet was first released in the United States in 2016 and later
aired in the United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and Russia/CIS.

14
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
The film explores themes of earth, space station, time lapse photography,
aerial photography, international space station (iss).
